const COVERS={
 "a1-00-prologo":"Dawn on a muddy track between bare hedgerows, early winter mist. A mounted knight in a worn surcoat rides ahead of a small band of horsemen, sword raised, at the instant his horse shies and rears beneath a leaning wooden post from which a single crow takes flight. Behind him the riders are only beginning to move. Low angle, long lens, frozen motion, mud thrown up by hooves.",
 "a1-01-camino":"Late afternoon, a wide wet plain under a low grey sky. A beaten file of seven travellers crosses left to right in silence, dirty bandages, lean horses, a banner rolled up without its pole: a captain on horseback, a young widow in dark wool, a young knight, a monk on foot, a stocky sergeant leading a mule loaded with a small chest and a blanket, a laundress, and a gaunt rider last with a gap before him. Far off in the valley, a fortified manor house with smoke rising from its chimney. Very wide shot, small figures against the land, standing water on the fields.",
 "a1-02-alto":"From a low hill, a brown swollen river with a crooked marker post at a ford, no bridge, no one crossing. In the foreground a monk in a black habit shakes his head while a weathered captain on horseback looks at him; the others wait behind with the mule. Overcast, wind bending the reeds.",
 "a1-03-colina":"Dusk, a column of travellers climbing a bare hillside path away from a river valley; the ford is a pale line far below. A laundress has slipped on the wet slope and a sergeant hands her the mule's halter without looking at her. Cold blue light, first stars, breath visible.",
 "camp-seq":"Night camp under bare trees, a dying fire of embers. A young knight talks with animation, his face lit orange, to a young widow who listens without expression; around them a stocky sergeant has stopped chewing, a monk holds a quill still over a wax tablet, a laundress keeps sewing. Deep darkness all around; only the fire lights the faces.",
 "a1-05-bertran":"Interior of a prosperous manor hall in winter, daylight through small windows and a fire. A broad, well-fed lord in his fifties, warm and hospitable, speaks with half a smile to a young widow seated across the table from him; a captain in mail stands by the door. Wine, bread, a crucifix on the wall, hounds asleep on the rushes.",
 "a1-06-aldea":"A village square of timber and daub houses with forty villagers gathered. A monk in a black habit kneels, one hand on a mother's shoulder, blessing a feverish child on a straw pallet. An old man at the front watches with his cap in his hands. Grey daylight, mud, chimney smoke.",
 "a1-08-obispo":"A bishop's audience hall with painted beams. A seated bishop in purple holds out a sealed letter to a young widow standing before him; behind him an official in black with a ledger, and five plain, respectable countrymen standing in a row. A weathered captain waits at the back. Candlelight mixed with grey daylight.",
 "a2-09-viuda":"The doorway of a poor cottage at the edge of a village in winter. A thin woman in her thirties, not dressed in mourning, speaks to the travellers from her threshold; in the foreground a stocky sergeant turns his face away while the young widow gives her a coin. A track leads out of frame toward a distant crossroads.",
 "a2-10-taberna":"A dim tavern at night, tallow light, low beams. A stocky sergeant with a cup in his hand leans across a rough table talking to a young knight, mid-sentence; the knight's face is stunned and still. The rest of the tavern is empty, benches upturned; only a tapster asleep in the far corner.",
 "a2-11-juramento":"Interior of a small stone parish church on a cold morning, breath visible. Before an altar with a reliquary and a signet ring laid on the cloth, twelve countrymen stand in a row with raised hands while an official in black reads from a book. To one side a well-dressed lord and his lawyer; to the other a young widow and her six companions. A young knight kneels alone in the middle of the nave, looking back at her.",
 "a2-12-bendicion":"A village lane at grey noon. A monk in a black habit stands with one hand on the bandaged arm of a wounded man sitting on a cart; the wounded man does not look at him. A grey-haired father stands by the cart, waiting, his face closing. Nothing is happening. Muddy light.",
 "a2-13-tres":"Night woods at the edge of a camp. Three figures argue in low voices by a lantern: a monk, a laundress and a stocky sergeant. In the foreground, out of their sight, a young widow in dark wool stands behind a tree trunk listening, her face half lit. Fireglow far behind.",
 "a2-14-sabia":"A cramped hut interior lit by a single oil lamp, herbs and small bones hanging from the beams. An old woman with a lined, knowing face scatters a handful of knucklebones and small carved stones on a cloth, talking with a practised smile, while a young widow sits across from her with a cold, composed face, silver coins stacked at her elbow. Smoke, low ceiling, dirt floor.",
 "a2-15-libro":"Night in the corner of a stable, a single candle. A young widow kneels over a blanket where knucklebones and small carved stones lie scattered; beside them a small manuscript book lies open at a crude ink drawing, more sign than picture, of a man hanging from a tree, and on the facing page a wheel of marks. Her finger rests on the page. Straw, and in the background a sleeping man with a fevered face.",
 "a2-17-tribunal":"A bishop's audience hall. A bishop in purple stays seated, not rising, as a young widow enters with six travel-stained companions; the bishop himself draws an old sealed charter back off the table toward him. Behind him, five plain countrymen stand apart and do not look at her. A great empty space between the widow and the throne. Cold light from tall windows.",
 "a3-18-ocupacion":"Late afternoon, a fortified stone manor house with a walled yard in a valley of winter fields. The young widow rides in through the open gate at the head of her six companions while an elderly steward runs off through a side gate, the dropped keys in the mud. A young knight rides first, standing in his stirrups. Long shadows.",
 "a3-19-cerco":"Night, the walled manor seen from its yard. A rope hangs from a high chamber window where shadows struggle; on the frosted flagstones below lies a young knight in a blue surcoat, fallen and still. Beyond the wall, the fires of a few dozen besiegers ring the house at a distance. Cold moonlight, breath visible, no one yet running toward him.",
 "a3-20-asalto":"The manor yard after an attack at dusk, the gate splintered and braced. A monk lies wounded on a cloak; a young widow kneels over him holding a small dark book while a laundress stands between them with her arm out, blocking her. A sergeant and a captain hold the gate behind. Smoke, cold light, blood on stone.",
 "a3-21-segundo":"Night, the manor's kitchen door on fire from outside. A captain in mail braces the burning door with his shoulder while flames climb the lintel beam above him; behind him a stocky sergeant, wounded, holds a lantern. Sparks, smoke, orange light on stone, shouts beyond the door.",
 "a3-22-agua":"Night. A young widow crouches at a stream below the manor, emptying something into the running water, her face lit from below by a shuttered lantern. A few steps above her on the bank, a gaunt man with a drawn knife keeps watch toward the besiegers' fires on the slope. Ice at the stream's edge, breath visible.",
 "a3-23-renaud":"Grey morning inside a manor with the siege gone, smoke hanging in the air. In the dark hollow beneath a wooden stair, a gaunt man with a blood-soaked side lies propped against the wall, holding the hand of a young widow in dark wool who kneels close to hear him, her face breaking. Around the hall beyond, four bodies under cloaks. Cold, still, ash.",
 "a3-24-noche":"Night in a vaulted manor cellar lit by a few candles. A young widow, exhausted, hair loose, sits on the stone floor with an open book, five shrouded bodies laid in a row on tables and the floor before her. Her face fills the frame, listening to something out of shot. On the sill of a small high window behind her, a crow, perfectly still. Total darkness beyond.",
 "a3-25-conde":"Winter morning, frost on the mud of a fortified manor's inner yard. The heavy inner gate has just swung open; in it stands a young widow in clean dark wool, hair bound, a single silver brooch at her shoulder, sinking to her knees in the mud. Before her, still mounted, a grey-bearded count in a travelling cloak over mail, with a long column of horsemen and a banner behind him. Arrows still stuck in the gate timbers, a scorched patch of earth. Far in the background, small and out of focus, five men repair a broken outer gate, their backs turned. Cold grey light.",
 "a3-26-copa":"A low, warm manor kitchen, a cold pot hanging in the hearth, firelight. A young widow in dark wool stands with her back half turned, holding a pewter cup; a single drop of blood falls from her pricked thumb into the wine, the silver brooch pin in her other hand. Behind her, unaware, a grey-bearded count in a travelling cloak waits; one soldier warms his hands at the fire with his back to her, another stands in the yard doorway looking out. Close, intimate, no one watching her.",
 "a3-27-bertran":"A frosty manor yard crowded with mounted soldiers under a count's banner. In the centre a grey-bearded count in a travelling cloak stands calm and unmoved, facing a portly man in his fifties in a good winter-stained cloak who argues with an open hand, a smaller troop of his own riders behind him. One step behind the count and to his left, a young widow in dark wool stands very still, dry-eyed, watching her uncle. A young captain at the count's side turns his head to look at his lord. Among the uncle's riders, at the back on a mule, a laundress in her thirties in a new cloak looks not at the lords but at the young widow. Far beyond the yard wall, five small figures stand motionless at a half-mended outer gate. Overcast winter light.",
 "a1-00-ahorcado":"Early winter afternoon at a muddy crossroads under a great bare tree. A body that has hung for days is half cut down, dangling by one arm from the rope, a ladder fallen beneath it. Two men in plain dark clothes with no colours have turned from it with drawn blades toward a small band coming round the bend: a knight in a worn surcoat, a captain, a stocky sergeant raising a crossbow, a monk, a laundress, a gaunt rider. Far up the opposite road, a young priest on a mule watches. Frozen ruts, low grey light, the instant before the clash.",
 "a3-28-doce":"A cold stone village church lit by two candles on the altar and the grey light from the door. Two well-cloaked men, clearly strangers of some standing, stand with their hands on a cloth-covered reliquary while a clerk writes in a ledger; one holds a sealed letter. A grey-bearded count watches from a chair; a portly lord and a thin procurator stand aside, the lord baffled. At the back among the village women, a thin woman in her thirties stares at the two men. A young widow in dark wool stands very still to one side.",
 "a3-29-mesa":"Night in a manor hall, a long oak table lit by a few candles. At its head, in a high-backed chair, a young widow in dark wool raises a pewter cup in a toast. Along both sides five still figures in shadow, their faces unlit, raise their cups with her; at the far end one place is empty. Painted beams above, the fire low.",
 "a3-30-carta":"A manor hall by grey daylight. A young widow in dark wool stands at a long oak table reading a letter with a broken red wax seal; beside it lies a small open manuscript book showing a drawing of a hanged man on a tree. Through the open door, in the yard, a young priest waits beside his mule, and far beyond the wall five indistinct figures work at a gate. Cold, quiet, still.",
 "a3-19-vela":"Night in a vaulted manor cellar lit by two candles. A young knight in a blue surcoat lies washed and still on a long table. A laundress and a young widow in dark wool tend the body together; a stocky sergeant sits on a barrel, half laughing as he talks; a captain listens standing; a monk in a black habit rests his hand on the head of one of the living. In the dark at the top of the cellar stair, a gaunt man sits awake watching the door. Warm, quiet, the one calm night.",
};
